WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.558 --> 00:00:04.147
- I spent a whole lifetime building this.

00:00:04.147 --> 00:00:04.980
And as long as I'm in charge,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.539
nobody's going to knock it down.

00:00:07.539 --> 00:00:10.109
They are cowards, that's
what they are, cowards.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.758
They switched the lights off.

00:00:12.758 --> 00:00:13.591
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:13.591 --> 00:00:14.846
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:14.846 --> 00:00:17.531
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:20.400
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.883
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:21.883 --> 00:00:23.611
we're going to learn from
the first prime minister

00:00:23.611 --> 00:00:25.312
of Singapore, Lee Kuan Yew,

00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:28.553
and my take on his top
ten rules to success.

00:00:28.553 --> 00:00:30.352
Rule number two is my personal favorite

00:00:30.352 --> 00:00:32.890
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.336
And as always as you're watching,

00:00:34.336 --> 00:00:36.538
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:36.538 --> 00:00:38.076
please leave it in the comments below.

00:00:38.076 --> 00:00:40.334
Put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired,

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.110
you might win a prize, as well.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.707
And also when you write it down,

00:00:43.707 --> 00:00:46.428
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself as well.

00:00:46.428 --> 00:00:47.261
Enjoy.

00:00:50.011 --> 00:00:53.178
(vibrant intro music)

00:04:33.002 --> 00:04:35.286
- I am quite determined.

00:04:35.286 --> 00:04:38.234
I may not be able to do it this way,

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:41.588
but don't believe I've given up.

00:04:41.588 --> 00:04:44.941
I will think of some
other way to get there.

00:04:44.941 --> 00:04:46.684
I think it's necessary

00:04:46.684 --> 00:04:49.894
because if you lack that determination,

00:04:49.894 --> 00:04:50.727
then you're not going to achieve.

00:04:50.727 --> 00:04:53.394
You will not be able to deliver.

00:04:55.538 --> 00:04:56.538
I am able to

00:04:57.772 --> 00:05:00.997
get ideas across to people in simple ways

00:05:00.997 --> 00:05:04.164
and persuade them to my point of view,

00:05:05.755 --> 00:05:08.180
if not the first time, then the second,

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:09.638
the third, the fourth time.

00:05:09.638 --> 00:05:10.971
I don't give up.

00:05:12.728 --> 00:05:14.724
Eventually I swing them around.

00:05:14.724 --> 00:05:17.141
Deng Xiaoping is a great man.

00:05:20.474 --> 00:05:22.765
He fought a great revolution.

00:05:22.765 --> 00:05:23.598
He saw

00:05:25.587 --> 00:05:29.004
the product of that revolution turn sour.

00:05:30.818 --> 00:05:32.845
He was fortunate to live long enough

00:05:32.845 --> 00:05:37.463
and he had the courage to
say, "No, we change course."

00:05:37.463 --> 00:05:38.546
"Let's learn.

00:05:39.503 --> 00:05:41.003
"Let's stop trying

00:05:42.143 --> 00:05:44.810
"to do everything by ourselves."

00:05:45.665 --> 00:05:50.530
So they started importing
and buying Boeing 707s.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.484
So they bought Tridents

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:56.455
instead of trying to
manufacture their own aircraft.

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:57.738
Eventually they will,

00:05:57.738 --> 00:06:01.571
but it will take two,
maybe three generations.

00:06:03.288 --> 00:06:05.088
That's how we succeeded

00:06:05.088 --> 00:06:07.338
because we have open minds,

00:06:09.276 --> 00:06:10.359
common sense.

00:06:11.879 --> 00:06:15.879
A lot of analysis, careful
weighing of the odds,

00:06:18.681 --> 00:06:20.914
make a firm decision,

00:06:20.914 --> 00:06:22.804
monitor it, implement it,

00:06:22.804 --> 00:06:24.887
modify, as it goes wrong.

00:06:27.289 --> 00:06:29.638
Abandon if it is no good.

00:06:29.638 --> 00:06:31.971
Life is what you make of it.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.917
You're dealt a pack of cards,

00:06:38.141 --> 00:06:42.224
your DNA is fixed by your
mother and your father.

00:06:44.401 --> 00:06:47.865
And even your siblings, but
you will get different parts

00:06:47.865 --> 00:06:49.698
of parcels of the DNA.

00:06:52.721 --> 00:06:55.054
Your job is to make the best

00:06:56.343 --> 00:06:59.760
of the cards that they handed out to you.

00:07:01.875 --> 00:07:05.085
What can you do well,
what can you not do well,

00:07:05.085 --> 00:07:06.918
what are you worst at?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.527
If you ask me to make
my living as a artist,

00:07:14.117 --> 00:07:15.034
I'll starve

00:07:17.876 --> 00:07:20.697
because I just can't draw.

00:07:20.697 --> 00:07:23.567
It wasn't in my father or my mother

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:27.150
or my great-grandfather's
or grandmother's.

00:07:28.715 --> 00:07:30.132
But if you ask me

00:07:35.441 --> 00:07:37.858
to do a mathematical question

00:07:42.386 --> 00:07:45.219
or to argue a point out, I get by.

00:07:48.638 --> 00:07:51.388
That's the cards I was handed out

00:07:52.437 --> 00:07:54.354
and I make use of them.

00:07:55.596 --> 00:07:58.289
Don't try and do something

00:07:58.289 --> 00:08:01.885
you are not favored by nature to do.

00:08:01.885 --> 00:08:06.312
I can tell you that when
I met the SIA pilots,

00:08:06.312 --> 00:08:10.479
I didn't meet them on TV,
I met them face-to-face,

00:08:11.682 --> 00:08:15.428
five feet across the
table, so they can see me

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:18.891
and see whether I'm still vigorous,

00:08:18.891 --> 00:08:21.724
able to campaign and take them on,

00:08:23.227 --> 00:08:26.155
whether it's worth taking me on.

00:08:26.155 --> 00:08:29.256
And I offered them two choices.

00:08:29.256 --> 00:08:33.006
Either you argue, you
stop this intimidation,

00:08:33.974 --> 00:08:37.807
which is what it was,
bringing SIA right down,

00:08:38.946 --> 00:08:43.128
disrupting services,
ruining its reputation.

00:08:43.128 --> 00:08:47.691
Millions of dollars worth
of advertisements and sales

00:08:47.691 --> 00:08:50.691
ruined within a matter of two weeks.

00:08:52.906 --> 00:08:54.656
I gave them a choice.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.403
Continue this

00:08:58.737 --> 00:08:59.654
and I will,

00:09:01.757 --> 00:09:05.444
by every means at my disposal, teach you

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:07.384
and get the people of Singapore,

00:09:07.384 --> 00:09:11.032
help me teach you a
lesson you won't forget.

00:09:11.032 --> 00:09:14.449
And I'm prepared to start all over again.

00:09:15.557 --> 00:09:19.640
Or stop it, get back to
work, restore discipline,

00:09:20.915 --> 00:09:22.665
then argue your case.

00:09:26.285 --> 00:09:27.952
Took them 65 minutes

00:09:32.093 --> 00:09:35.355
and they decided, okay,
it isn't worth the fight.

00:09:35.355 --> 00:09:36.188
Why?

00:09:37.608 --> 00:09:40.191
Because they know they'll lose.

00:09:41.333 --> 00:09:43.779
They know that I'm prepared
to drown the airline

00:09:43.779 --> 00:09:46.546
and they know that I can
get the airline going again

00:09:46.546 --> 00:09:47.629
without them.

00:09:49.176 --> 00:09:51.162
And let there be no mistakes about this.

00:09:51.162 --> 00:09:55.329
Whoever governs Singapore
must have that iron in him

00:09:56.182 --> 00:09:57.477
or give it up.

00:09:57.477 --> 00:09:59.663
This is not a game of cards.

00:09:59.663 --> 00:10:01.462
This is your life and mine.

00:10:01.462 --> 00:10:04.774
I spent a whole lifetime building this.

00:10:04.774 --> 00:10:06.813
And as long as I'm in charge,

00:10:06.813 --> 00:10:08.949
nobody's going to knock it down.

00:10:08.949 --> 00:10:11.099
We have so much at stake.

00:10:11.099 --> 00:10:14.599
We have gone so far to secure the country.

00:10:15.795 --> 00:10:19.370
I say rally around and
keep these evil forces--

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:22.220
You see, they are so
ashamed of themselves,

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.370
they have switched the light off.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.453
Look at that.

00:10:26.395 --> 00:10:30.024
They are cowards, that's
what they are, cowards.

00:10:30.024 --> 00:10:32.263
They switched the lights off.

00:10:32.263 --> 00:10:34.513
(applause)

00:10:36.216 --> 00:10:37.299
Look at that.

00:10:38.633 --> 00:10:41.183
Are these men who are going to lead you

00:10:41.183 --> 00:10:43.362
to peace and prosperity

00:10:43.362 --> 00:10:46.599
or to ruination and position?

00:10:46.599 --> 00:10:48.849
(applause)

00:10:50.314 --> 00:10:51.314
Look at that

00:10:52.972 --> 00:10:55.931
God knows what they're doing in the dark.

00:10:55.931 --> 00:10:58.181
(applause)

00:11:00.242 --> 00:11:01.809
And I say this,

00:11:01.809 --> 00:11:05.309
they succeed on the basis of intimidation.

00:11:07.173 --> 00:11:08.006
And I say

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:13.507
that they make the error that
we are easily intimidated,

00:11:15.577 --> 00:11:18.419
then they have a lot to be sorry for

00:11:18.419 --> 00:11:21.643
because you know we have so much at stake,

00:11:21.643 --> 00:11:24.540
we can't afford to be intimidated.

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:27.007
- Why do you have so
little faith in the ability

00:11:27.007 --> 00:11:29.757
of your people, so well-educated,

00:11:30.699 --> 00:11:34.487
to make intelligent
judgements on diversity

00:11:34.487 --> 00:11:36.737
of ideas on competing news?

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:42.357
- I have been in office for now 29 years.

00:11:44.149 --> 00:11:48.316
I've won seven general elections
since my first in 1959.

00:11:50.452 --> 00:11:54.619
I think that qualifies me
at least to be able to say

00:11:55.481 --> 00:11:59.089
that I do know Singapore
better than the questioner.

00:11:59.089 --> 00:12:02.422
Your father and grandfather's generation

00:12:03.757 --> 00:12:05.257
lived a hard life.

00:12:10.061 --> 00:12:13.916
Very few people had homes of their own.

00:12:13.916 --> 00:12:14.999
In Chinatown,

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:22.107
you have cubicles, eight
or ten people in the room

00:12:25.096 --> 00:12:26.596
sharing four bunks

00:12:29.204 --> 00:12:32.454
because they do shift work, save money.

00:12:35.864 --> 00:12:40.373
If you lived in those
conditions and you get a flat,

00:12:40.373 --> 00:12:43.083
one room, which is what we started with,

00:12:43.083 --> 00:12:45.507
communal bathroom, communal kitchen,

00:12:45.507 --> 00:12:48.424
running hot and cold, water closet.

00:12:49.865 --> 00:12:53.282
That's from the lowest depths of the ship

00:12:54.982 --> 00:12:59.805
to a deck with a window with
a porthole and air coming in.

00:12:59.805 --> 00:13:01.730
And from that, to go to a three-room

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:03.933
or four-room or five-room flat,

00:13:03.933 --> 00:13:06.459
you go up to the higher
levels of the ship.

00:13:06.459 --> 00:13:09.777
And finally now, we've got
executive flats and condominiums

00:13:09.777 --> 00:13:13.944
that means you're on a
cruise ship at the very top.

00:13:16.389 --> 00:13:20.056
Now, I have watched my
grandchildren grow up

00:13:21.543 --> 00:13:25.293
and they are growing up
much more comfortably

00:13:26.564 --> 00:13:27.981
than my children.

00:13:29.461 --> 00:13:33.628
My wife and I made sure that
they became self-reliant

00:13:35.494 --> 00:13:39.188
and not somebody will pick
up their balls for them.

00:13:39.188 --> 00:13:43.304
As Prime Minister, I was
given a house at Sri Temasek,

00:13:43.304 --> 00:13:45.628
so I took them there one day to play,

00:13:45.628 --> 00:13:48.174
and Sri Temasek's on high ground,

00:13:48.174 --> 00:13:52.478
they're playing with a
ball, the ball rolled down.

00:13:52.478 --> 00:13:53.978
And the butler ran

00:13:55.782 --> 00:13:59.949
50 or 60 yards to pick up
the ball and bring it back.

00:14:01.399 --> 00:14:02.990
My wife and I watched that and said,

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:07.040
"Oh no, if we stay here for five years,

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:11.207
"my children grow up believing
that life is like that,

00:14:12.184 --> 00:14:15.535
"that somebody will always
pick up balls for them."

00:14:15.535 --> 00:14:17.487
We stay at home.

00:14:17.487 --> 00:14:19.744
And I think that's been good for them.

00:14:19.744 --> 00:14:22.781
And that is a problem we face today.

00:14:22.781 --> 00:14:26.948
Many of the parents who aren't
this [Inaudible: 00:14:27],

00:14:30.005 --> 00:14:33.261
started like the people in Chinatown.

00:14:33.261 --> 00:14:36.428
They understand what it is to be poor.

00:14:37.696 --> 00:14:41.262
Today's children do not
understand what it is to be poor.

00:14:41.262 --> 00:14:45.429
But, you can intellectually
and emotionally understand

00:14:47.673 --> 00:14:50.981
if we don't make the same effort,

00:14:50.981 --> 00:14:53.037
you go back to where you were.

00:14:53.037 --> 00:14:54.376
We made mistakes.

00:14:54.376 --> 00:14:58.376
We put money in [Yoo-Pock:
00:14:55], in Jurong,

00:15:00.148 --> 00:15:01.349
second-hand machinery.

00:15:01.349 --> 00:15:03.069
We were young then, we
were new in the game.

00:15:03.069 --> 00:15:05.840
They sold a second-hand
machine, we didn't know.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.007
We lost money.

00:15:08.736 --> 00:15:11.403
We wrote it off, but we learned.

00:15:12.532 --> 00:15:15.182
Human beings are not like computers.

00:15:15.182 --> 00:15:17.475
You know, you can take one computer bank,

00:15:17.475 --> 00:15:20.872
plug the terminals, and all
the data from one computer bank

00:15:20.872 --> 00:15:22.539
can go into another.

00:15:23.973 --> 00:15:26.813
But human beings start with fresh minds.

00:15:26.813 --> 00:15:30.601
You get a newborn child, he grows up.

00:15:30.601 --> 00:15:32.018
Completely blank.

00:15:34.166 --> 00:15:38.333
Input from parents, input from
friends, input from teachers.

00:15:40.453 --> 00:15:44.685
But no input is as vivid, as long-lasting,

00:15:44.685 --> 00:15:47.237
as his own experience.

00:15:47.237 --> 00:15:50.404
I'd rather strut my inner motivations,

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.773
my proclivities.

00:15:55.536 --> 00:15:59.703
If you want me to have a go,
I would say I'm consistent.

00:16:02.099 --> 00:16:04.349
I don't say one thing today

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.546
and another tomorrow and change again

00:16:08.546 --> 00:16:10.245
the day after tomorrow.

00:16:10.245 --> 00:16:12.662
It's not that I'm inflexible.

00:16:13.533 --> 00:16:15.950
There are circumstances where

00:16:17.911 --> 00:16:21.503
the situation is altered
and I'm prepared to say,

00:16:21.503 --> 00:16:24.098
well, this no long applies,

00:16:24.098 --> 00:16:27.015
but on the whole I stay consistent.

00:16:30.289 --> 00:16:34.456
I had three journalists write
up a book on my speeches.

00:16:37.159 --> 00:16:39.159
I asked them at the end,

00:16:40.591 --> 00:16:43.924
"What was the dominant theme you found?"

00:16:45.419 --> 00:16:48.356
And the three of them said,

00:16:48.356 --> 00:16:52.523
"Consistency throughout all
of 40 years in public eye."

00:16:53.439 --> 00:16:57.606
What I said at the beginning
throughout all that period,

00:16:59.516 --> 00:17:02.183
the theme stayed loud and clear.

00:17:04.584 --> 00:17:05.507
I don't mean it's simple

00:17:05.507 --> 00:17:07.173
because you know where you stand with me

00:17:07.173 --> 00:17:09.756
and you know what I want to do.

00:17:34.296 --> 00:17:37.296
You see, the whole of my adult life,

00:17:45.247 --> 00:17:48.080
I had believed in Malaysian merger

00:17:50.945 --> 00:17:54.195
and the unity of these two territories.

00:17:57.432 --> 00:18:00.182
You know, it's a people connected

00:18:01.873 --> 00:18:02.956
by geography,

00:18:05.425 --> 00:18:06.258
economics,

00:18:09.029 --> 00:18:10.696
and ties of kinship.

00:18:21.475 --> 00:18:24.558
Will you mind if we stop for a while?

00:18:55.123 --> 00:18:56.470
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:19:00.148
I made this video because
Amit Gupta asked me to.

00:19:00.148 --> 00:19:00.981
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:19:00.981 --> 00:19:02.324
that you want me to profile next,

00:19:02.324 --> 00:19:03.540
check out the link in the description

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:06.047
and you can go and cast your vote.

00:19:06.047 --> 00:19:07.826
I'd also love to know which
clip resonated the most

00:19:07.826 --> 00:19:08.659
with you,

00:19:08.659 --> 00:19:10.293
what lesson are you going
to take from this video

00:19:10.293 --> 00:19:12.378
and immediately apply to your life

00:19:12.378 --> 00:19:13.869
or to your business somehow.

00:19:13.869 --> 00:19:15.239
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:19:15.239 --> 00:19:17.454
I'm really curious to find
out what you have to say.

00:19:17.454 --> 00:19:19.769
I also want to give a
quick trick to Brian Tracy.

00:19:19.769 --> 00:19:21.854
Brian, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:19:21.854 --> 00:19:24.276
of my book, Your One Word,
and posting the review

00:19:24.276 --> 00:19:25.680
on your Facebook page.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.080
I really, really, really
appreciate the support

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.990
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed my book.

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:31.526
Thank you you guys so much for watching.

00:19:31.526 --> 00:19:32.729
I believe in you.

00:19:32.729 --> 00:19:34.565
I hope we can take you
to believe in yourself

00:19:34.565 --> 00:19:36.969
and whatever your one word is.

00:19:36.969 --> 00:19:39.386
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:19:45.564 --> 00:19:47.428
- What's the most important change,

00:19:47.428 --> 00:19:49.405
or most significant change
in your way of thinking

00:19:49.405 --> 00:19:51.822
about the world over the last

00:19:54.423 --> 00:19:55.256
20 years?

00:19:58.851 --> 00:20:01.601
- That the impossible can happen.

00:20:02.587 --> 00:20:05.120
I never thought that the Soviet Union

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.120
would improve so easily.

00:20:08.725 --> 00:20:12.892
And I never thought that
the Chinese would abandon

00:20:15.371 --> 00:20:17.405
the communist system

00:20:17.405 --> 00:20:20.822
and move into the free market so readily.

00:20:22.833 --> 00:20:25.500
It was unthinkable 20 years ago.

00:20:27.176 --> 00:20:30.593
Both has happened, the world has changed.

00:20:31.874 --> 00:20:34.286
- And it's not clear exactly
how it's all going to--

00:20:34.286 --> 00:20:38.872
- No, it is not exactly
clear when it will happen.

00:20:38.872 --> 00:20:40.281
- [Interviewer] Exactly.

00:20:40.281 --> 00:20:43.404
- But that it will happen
now in the long-term.

00:20:43.404 --> 00:20:45.154
50 to 100 years, yes.

00:20:46.082 --> 00:20:46.915
- [Interviewer] And the center of gravity

00:20:46.915 --> 00:20:48.920
is shifting to Asia.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.694
- It must be because
the population's there.

00:20:51.694 --> 00:20:55.446
The talent pool of 1.3 billion people,

00:20:55.446 --> 00:20:57.040
plus the Japanese, the Koreans,

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:59.623
the Vietnamese, and the others,

00:21:00.506 --> 00:21:03.256
it can match Europe and America.

00:21:04.394 --> 00:21:06.807
But that talent pool was inert,

00:21:06.807 --> 00:21:09.181
did not have science and technology,

00:21:09.181 --> 00:21:12.385
did not care about science and technology.

00:21:12.385 --> 00:21:15.052
But now, everything that you do,

00:21:17.013 --> 00:21:18.096
Asia's doing.

00:21:19.113 --> 00:21:22.683
I ignore polling as a
method of government.

00:21:22.683 --> 00:21:26.516
I think that shows a
certain weakness of mind,

00:21:28.538 --> 00:21:31.121
an inability to chart a course.

00:21:32.309 --> 00:21:33.663
Whichever way the wind blows,

00:21:33.663 --> 00:21:37.603
whichever way the media
encourages the people to go,

00:21:37.603 --> 00:21:38.762
you follow.

00:21:38.762 --> 00:21:40.970
You are not a leader.

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:43.576
If your message is one of despair,

00:21:43.576 --> 00:21:46.243
then you should not be a leader.

00:21:47.988 --> 00:21:50.155
You must give people hope,

00:21:52.516 --> 00:21:56.067
hope of improving their condition.

00:21:56.067 --> 00:22:00.434
There are moments, of course,
when you feel very down,

00:22:00.434 --> 00:22:03.843
either because you're physically
down or emotionally down

00:22:03.843 --> 00:22:07.618
or because the world has
turned adverse against you.

00:22:07.618 --> 00:22:11.014
I think when you are in that condition,

00:22:11.014 --> 00:22:15.181
the first thing you do is
to get a good night's sleep.

00:22:17.222 --> 00:22:19.889
Then get a swim or chase a ball,

00:22:20.928 --> 00:22:23.678
get the cobwebs out of your mind.

00:22:24.696 --> 00:22:27.196
I believe, and I practice this

00:22:28.785 --> 00:22:31.452
for all these years in politics,

00:22:33.126 --> 00:22:36.738
that if you are not fit,
you're going to make mistakes.

00:22:36.738 --> 00:22:37.571
Physically fit.

00:22:37.571 --> 00:22:41.071
You must stay physically and mentally fit.

00:22:43.374 --> 00:22:45.041
I exercise everyday.

00:22:46.560 --> 00:22:49.143
I used to jog, swim, play golf.

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:52.843
Golf more for relaxation,

00:22:52.843 --> 00:22:56.926
just to get away from the
smoky conference rooms.

00:22:59.342 --> 00:23:02.509
And it's part of the balance you keep.

00:23:06.463 --> 00:23:09.880
Now, I cycle, I swim, even when I travel.

00:23:13.589 --> 00:23:16.422
And since the last 10 years or so,

00:23:18.337 --> 00:23:20.337
I've learned to meditate

00:23:22.255 --> 00:23:25.672
because it's one way of calming yourself.

00:23:29.571 --> 00:23:30.848
It takes practice.

00:23:30.848 --> 00:23:32.226
I had a doctor teach me.

00:23:32.226 --> 00:23:33.513
He was a Buddhist.

00:23:33.513 --> 00:23:36.786
He retired and he spends his time

00:23:36.786 --> 00:23:38.880
helping people to meditate,

00:23:38.880 --> 00:23:41.276
especially those with calming in lessons.

00:23:41.276 --> 00:23:43.776
You know, to take life calmly.

00:23:45.449 --> 00:23:49.610
And I think at the end of say,
20 minutes to half an hour,

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:51.443
my pulse rate can down

00:23:53.602 --> 00:23:55.352
from 100 to about 60.

00:23:57.154 --> 00:24:00.514
I mean, you can feel yourself subside.

00:24:00.514 --> 00:24:04.514
I mean you still your
mind, you empty your mind.

00:24:07.926 --> 00:24:09.926
Then when you're rested,

00:24:13.547 --> 00:24:15.130
you resume quietly.

00:24:17.809 --> 00:24:19.547
If you've still got the same problems,

00:24:19.547 --> 00:24:21.380
maybe you sleep on it,

00:24:22.985 --> 00:24:26.092
come back, look at it for a days

00:24:26.092 --> 00:24:30.625
then decide maybe there's
a better way of solving it

00:24:30.625 --> 00:24:33.958
or talk to some friends, get some ideas.

00:24:35.257 --> 00:24:39.612
But if you are not in good shape,
you're going to make mistakes

00:24:39.612 --> 00:24:41.529
and that's disastrous.

